  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "The netlist implements exactly the architecture the specification describes (24V→5V buck U7/TPS62933 → 5V→3.3V LDO U9/AZ1117; two ADM3260 isolators U2/U6 bridging the main I2C to the isolated pH/EC EZO circuits while the RTD EZO M2 shares the non-isolated bus; three TMC2209 drivers U8/U10/U11 on a shared single-wire UART with per-driver 5VOUT current-reference dividers and 110 mΩ sense resistors; IRLR2905 main-pump and N-MOSFET ATO-valve low-side switches with BT3904 interlocks; SMBJ28A TVS and 7 A fuse on the 24 V input). All apparent differences from the spec's component table (M1↔M4, U3/U4↔U2/U6, U5–U7↔U8/U10/U11, L1↔L2, F1↔F2, D2↔D1, etc.) are the reference-number permutations the spec itself documents, and the unwired TF-Luna, DNP BME280/BH1750, missing DS18B20 net, and firmware-GPIO mismatch are explicitly listed as known limitations, not faults. Passive values, ratings, pull directions (e.g. valve gate pull-down R49 to GND) and the ADM3260 VSEL divider (R46/R4 and R30/R48, which biases VSEL above the high threshold to select the isolated +5 V the EZO circuits need) are all consistent with the intended design, so no anomaly is supported by the files."
